  "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\u2016kw\u2016=|k|\\cdot \u2016w\u2016\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016-\\frac{w}{5}\u2016 & =|-\\frac{1}{5}|\\cdot \u2016w\u2016 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{4+16+4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
